    "active": true,
    "description": "<p><strong>CLASS TYPE</strong> Adept</p>\n<p>Mystics follow ancient traditions of meditation, spiritual awareness and inner discipline. Many cultures describe the sensations produced by these practices as chi: a vital current linking body, mind and spirit. In rules terms, however, a Mystic does not possess a chi pool. Their extraordinary abilities are represented by techniques with the Focus trait and by innate spells.</p>\n<p>Unlike conventional spellcasters, Mystics do not prepare spells or spend PP on the magic granted by their class. Their meditative disciplines awaken magic as an innate part of the self. These innate spells use the normal TRG Prime rules for innate magic and become expended after use when they possess the Focus trait.</p>\n<p><strong>MAGICAL TRADITION</strong> Your class magic is innate rather than conventional spellcasting. The magical tradition and magical ability score of your Mystic spells are determined by your Monastic Path.</p>",
    "classType": "Adept",
    "keyAbilityScores": "Wisdom (min +2), Dexterity, Constitution",
    "classSkills": "Acrobatics, Artistry, Athletics, Climbing, Culture, Medicine, Meditation, Mental Focus, Perception, Power Manipulation, Sense Motive",
    "grantedFeats": "1: Inner Discipline",
    "classAbilities": "1: Alter the Thread, 1: Mystical Discipline, 1: Mystical Power, 1: Mystical Resolve, 1: Monastic Path",
    "proficiencies": "You may use all simple weapons, monastic weapons and light armour.",
